    Call 1: ('In lcms/src/cmsio0.c, what is the best compatibility condition for creating TagLinked entries in _cmsReadHeader for two directory tags sharing offset and size? Please inspect tag descriptors and built-in descriptor registrations, and identify whether equality of supported type sets and ElemCount is appropriate, or whether checking a common actual on-disk type is sufficient. Note legitimate linked-tag use cases that must remain supported.', "The vulnerability is an offset-based alias between cmsSigViewingConditionsTag ('view') and cmsSigGamutTag ('gamt'). Both share an offset/size whose payload is LUT8. _cmsReadHeader currently links solely by offset/size at lines 795-803. cmsReadTag(gamt) follows to the view directory slot, validates LUT8 against the requested gamt descriptor, decodes cmsPipeline into view storage, and SaveTags later writes that pointer according to view, causing an invalid cast. I need a root-cause patch restricted to lcms C/C++ source. I am considering a helper that compares _cmsGetTagDescriptor results before setting TagLinked, likely requiring compatible supported type signatures and element counts, but need to preserve legitimate ICC shared-data tags.")...
